  "notes": "Distinct from the homophones {打|う}つ (to hit, to strike physically) and {撃|う}つ (to shoot). {討|う}つ specifically means to attack and defeat an enemy, often with a connotation of justice or retribution.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {敵|てき}を{討|う}つ (to strike down the enemy)\n- {仇|かたき}を{討|う}つ (to take revenge)\n- {賊|ぞく}を{討|う}つ (to subjugate bandits)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {討伐|とうばつ} — subjugation, punitive expedition\n- {仇討|あだう}ち — revenge, vendetta\n- {討論|とうろん} — debate (different usage of {討|とう})\n\nPrimarily used in historical and literary contexts. In modern usage, {仇|かたき}を{討|う}つ survives as a set phrase.",
